@node Methodology
@section Methodology
@cindex benchmark methodology

Each port was run @strong{100 times} against a large input file
containing 2,289,195 lines of file path data.  Program output was
discarded; only timing metrics were captured using:

@example
/usr/bin/time -f "real=%e user=%U sys=%S mem=%M" \
    psort_c < /tmp/find.data > /dev/null
@end example

Metrics collected per run:

@table @var
@item real
Wall-clock elapsed time, in seconds.
@item user
User-space CPU time, in seconds.
@item sys
Kernel (system-call) CPU time, in seconds.
@item mem
Peak resident set size (@samp{%M} from @command{time}), in kilobytes.
@end table

Statistics reported: minimum, maximum, mean, and population standard
deviation (n@tie{}=@tie{}100 runs per variant).

