@node RPM Installation
@section RPM (Fedora / RHEL / CentOS)
@cindex RPM
@cindex rpmbuild

@example
# Create a source tarball from the repository
git archive --prefix=psort-1.0.0/ HEAD \
    | gzip > ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES/psort-1.0.0.tar.gz

# Build the RPM
rpmbuild -ba psort.spec

# Install
rpm -i ~/rpmbuild/RPMS/$(uname -m)/psort-1.0.0-1.*.rpm
@end example

After installation @command{psort} points to @command{psort_c} by
default.  To switch:

@example
update-alternatives --config psort
@end example

@node Debian Installation
@section Debian / Ubuntu
@cindex Debian package
@cindex dpkg-buildpackage

@example
dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
sudo dpkg -i ../psort_1.0.0-1_$(dpkg --print-architecture).deb
@end example

@node Manual Installation
@section Manual Installation
@cindex manual installation

@example
sudo install -m755 psort_c psort_go psort.py psort.pl /usr/local/bin/
sudo install -m644 psort.1   /usr/local/share/man/man1/
sudo install -m644 psort.info /usr/local/share/info/
sudo install-info /usr/local/share/info/psort.info \
    /usr/local/share/info/dir
@end example

